      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10908794::web::037::microstructure_investigation",
        "PMC9960858::web::020::3_4_worn_track_morphology_and_wear_mecha"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "A stable Cr-enriched oxide layer improves the high-temperature wear resistance of FeNiCrCoCu coatings.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10908794::web::037::microstructure_investigation",
        "PMC9960858::web::020::3_4_worn_track_morphology_and_wear_mecha"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modification causes rapid formation of the Cr-enriched oxide film at elevated temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10908794::web::037::microstructure_investigation"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide layer limits direct metal-to-metal contact.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9960858::web::020::3_4_worn_track_morphology_and_wear_mecha"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide layer decreases adhesive wear and shifts the dominant mechanism from severe adhesive wear toward milder oxidative wear.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9960858::web::020::3_4_worn_track_morphology_and_wear_mecha"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "An oxide layer on the worn surface can act as a lubricating layer and reduce friction under high normal load.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9960858::web::020::3_4_worn_track_morphology_and_wear_mecha"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The shift toward oxidative wear reduces material removal.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An oxide layer that is more resistant to rupture produces better wear resistance.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9960858::web::020::3_4_worn_track_morphology_and_wear_mecha"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
